WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
The second thing that changes
is the size of the job.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:06.112
Most migration plans
count users and groups.

3
00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:11.534
But Active Directory has also been
holding the rest of the estate together:

4
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:17.218
DNS and DHCP, the certificate services
behind smart cards, Wi-Fi, VPN and servers,

5
00:00:17.218 --> 00:00:20.803
RADIUS sign-in, applications
that bind over LDAP,

6
00:00:20.803 --> 00:00:26.050
the sync engine itself, domain-joined
devices, time, and file permissions.

7
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.050
You don't need to memorize the list.

8
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:32.188
The point is that none of it moves
just because users sync to the cloud.

9
00:00:32.188 --> 00:00:36.713
Some interim steps, like the
NPS extension for Entra MFA,

10
00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:39.763
are useful, but they still depend on AD.

11
00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:43.576
So the program gives each
dependency its own adapter:

12
00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.476
an owner, a target, a cutover
test and a validation check.

13
00:00:47.476 --> 00:00:50.850
And they retire in priority
order, not all at once.

14
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.440
Next, delegation.
